WEBVTT

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:09.660
to the devil and the dive bomber and you're diving with it you gotta change your direction

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:15.630
you gotta zoom up again the lord knows your hidden sins and that's any kind of sin brother

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:25.540
what did the great prophet isaiah say he may see you gotta make the lord you see an eye just

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.840
as he is mine i can see a better world a greater world

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.310
Every man shall bear his own burden.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.790
Whatsoever a man saweth, that shall he also reach.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:45.360
Ask yourself if you can answer one thing.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:52.310
How much is each of you guilty for a devil in the world to do?

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:32.440
Mister, what do you want?

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.300
You going to Santa Sierra?

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:35.800
No riders.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:44.480
Come on, get in.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:18.150
Huh?

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:51.670
The kind of Sierra, huh? You ever been there before?

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:59.520
I live there. I was looking for work.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:02.710
I heard they were taking our hands at that chemical plant.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:04.450
They weren't.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:05.150
It's rough.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.060
Maybe you ought to try up north.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:07.740
Oregon.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.330
Maybe you'd do better up there.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.690
No, I've got to stay where I am.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:13.980
I've got a wife and a kid.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:15.790
Another one on the way.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.250
They sure drop the net over you, don't they?

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.560
Nobody jumped up and asked me, but I figure when a guy gets married young, he can just as soon go out and cut his throat.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:38.090
Why they should let a guy get a marriage license before they let him vote?

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:38.850
It's criminal.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.160
Leave it to the female gender.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.880
They hook you before you get good sense.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.710
Now, you take my old lady, and I'm not kidding.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:46.750
You want her, you can have her.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.170
Hey, fella, you're home.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:56.290
So long.

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:57.590
Good luck to you.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:03:59.160
Thanks.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:23.010
That's not his bill.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:35.360
Tommy, please.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:44.110
Tommy, stop that.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.240
Then I'll always go.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:47.880
Oh, yes, you will.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.510
Now sit that whining and put your shoe on.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:51.920
Put it on.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.420
When you get back, we'll go for a walk.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:56.240
Maybe to the zoo.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:57.760
I don't want to go to know.

00:04:58.320 --> 00:04:59.980
All right, Tommy, have it yours.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.120
I didn't hear you coming.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:08.660
How are you, darling?

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:09.490
Fine.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.370
Can I have a quarter pop?

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:12.730
You look tired.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.330
I didn't get much sleep last night.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.700
The club is going to the baseball and it costs a quarter.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.240
All the other kids are going.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.890
Oh, there you are. Here, well, let's do it.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:25.450
Fifty-six!

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.270
You got a job.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:29.970
You go to that bar.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.400
All game, buy yourself a couple of hot dogs.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:32.820
Gee, Pop, thanks a lot.

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:34.270
My mom, I'm late.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:35.960
Tell me what happened.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:36.720
Did you go to the doctor?

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.240
Oh, never mind about that.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:39.340
Tell me about the job.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.570
Oh, Judy, honey, you promised me.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.600
They've got good doctors at that clinic.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:48.720
They're the best in town.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.320
I don't really need a doctor yet.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.880
Anyhow, I knew you'd get a job.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.000
And then we could pay for my own doctor.

00:05:58.150 --> 00:05:59.390
Oh, tell me what happened.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:05:59.970
Tell me.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.740
Tell me about the job.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.040
There isn't any job.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:10.660
You just gave Tommy a half a dollar.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:12.290
What did you do that for?

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:14.010
Because I wanted to.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:18.340
Yes, I wanted to.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.610
My kid can go to a baseball game, can't he?

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.660
Not when we owe money for groceries.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:26.660
Last night, I needed 50 cents more to buy eggs.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:27.560
Then we'll do without them.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:29.540
Judy, honey, don't pick on me now. I'm tired.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:33.540
Begging for groceries. Begging for doctors.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.220
Is that what we came to California for?

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:37.350
You know what we came to California for?

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.070
You wanted to come as much as I did?

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:41.990
And I'd help it if a million other guys had the same idea?

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:46.800
Well, I wish we were back home. At least we weren't beggars.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:51.880
Judy, don't cry. Please don't cry.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:58.120
What can I do? What do you want me to do?

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:41.370
Sautéed, tender, then add the wine.

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:42.350
On a low flame.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:42.730
Gotcha.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:44.840
Tonight I'm going to have veal scallopini.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.740
Peany for paradise, Mike.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.360
You get tired of writing that newspaper column, I got a napoleon that'll fit you.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:50.800
You're a natural-born chef.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.610
Excuse me while I get this jerk.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:55.000
A bottle of beer?

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:56.740
I love what you wrote in your column yesterday.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.720
How do you like that, a priest helping Indians fight about the virus?

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.740
This must have been a town in those days.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:03.440
Where do you dig up all your info?

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:05.380
You said it might dig.

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:10.810
To write a newspaper column, you need a good public librarian, a strong typewriter, and an occasional idea.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:13.940
How many newspapers you call him in, Mr. Stanton? A couple of hundred?

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:14.920
Something like that.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.410
Hey, you're a dime short. Eastern beer's two bits.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:20.760
I didn't want Eastern beer.

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:21.820
Why didn't you say so?

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:22.560
Why didn't you ask me?

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:29.980
This Mr. Stanton.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.500
Stanton, you take a beer drinker, you got a jerk.

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:35.960
I don't know, Mike. The Lord must love the beer drinker.

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.890
He made an awful lot of them. See ya.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:56.350
Okay, kid. That's enough.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:07.080
See if any sea pair of shoes back there?

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:10.920
These?

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:21.840
Yeah, shoe went rolling down the goodies.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:23.290
Must be getting rusty.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:25.210
Nothing wrong with that last one.

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:26.290
Yeah, it was all right.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:28.780
Joe?

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:29.960
No, no, no.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:36.980
But it still ain't my money game, flingin' a bowl for 25, 50 bucks a line.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:40.850
I better sharpen up. Come on, help yourself. Why pay bar prices?

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:42.440
Oh, no, thanks. The beer is okay.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:45.210
Make a boiler maker out of it. It's all beer's good for it.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:48.180
It's sure been a long time since I had one of these.

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:53.180
Oh, it's fine, will ya?

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:56.540
Oh.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.980
Well, no outfit, I guess. I never got out of Camp Roberts.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:06.530
Roberts? What do you know? I took my basic there.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.110
No kidding?

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:10.430
Yeah. What a joint. Couldn't wait to get shipped over.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:11.550
You got over, huh?

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:12.170
Yeah.

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:13.590
Pretty rugged, huh?

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:16.070
There was a rumor I heard in Paris.

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:19.050
Paris. Ooh la la.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:23.120
You know what you could get for one crummy pack of cigarettes?

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:25.100
Boy, the markup was terrific.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:29.490
Sure wish a guy could get a buck that easy these days.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:31.190
Things are kind of slow, huh?

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:35.250
Yeah, they're up and down. They're mostly down.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.390
It's kind of tough getting anything steady.

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:42.620
You can drive a car, can't you?

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:43.680
Yeah.

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:46.200
Walk me over to my hotel.

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:47.080
Well?

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:48.720
Hey, come on, come on. It's only a couple of blocks.

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:50.570
Maybe I can put you on to something.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:51.830
Okay, sure.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:52.870
Yeah, hold this one, will you?

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:54.680
Hey, what's your name?

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:56.410
Tyler. Howard Tyler.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:57.500
Tyler, huh?

00:10:59.020 --> 00:10:59.740
Where are you from, Howard?

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:01.890
Boston, Boston.

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:10.490
Don't air pressure, will you, Helen?

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:17.420
Oh, these days I'm gonna go back to Berlin.

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:27.060
But, you know, you never could decide between those big German frollies.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:29.350
Dullies.

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:32.600
I give them all the same break.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:38.400
Hey, did you ever notice one thing all women have in common?

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:41.170
They're all partial of the same color, kareem.

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:42.810
Yeah, I know what you mean.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:45.400
Not bad, huh?

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:46.750
Eau de nuit.

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:49.220
Why, that smells good.

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:50.680
Ah, it smells expensive.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:52.480
$6.50 a bottle.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:55.540
That guy's gotta keep himself in shape.

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:57.760
I used to play a little handball at the Y.

00:11:58.220 --> 00:11:59.740
You never know when you're gonna get in a beef.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:04.310
Hey, what size color you wear?

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:06.720
Fifteen and a half.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:08.960
It's a van.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.580
None of these I could spare you, but...

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.320
Our silk makes my skin itch.

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:17.450
Fast that fella, will ya?

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:24.740
Platinum, you know, not silver.

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:26.840
Well, you sure treat yourself all right.

00:12:26.980 --> 00:12:27.580
Yeah, they're pretty good.

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:28.680
Hey, you think I need shave?

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:29.820
No, no.

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:38.020
Jerry, got any idea what time it's getting to be?

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:44.570
5.30. What? Going to the blood?

00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:48.390
Well, I gotta get home. Jerry, about that job you mentioned.

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:50.140
My wife doesn't know where I am.

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:52.560
Keep a guess, and they respect you more that way.

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:56.370
Hey, you like this one? Oh, yeah, that's good.

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:58.850
Uh, Jerry... What do you mind giving to me?

00:12:59.640 --> 00:12:59.980
I like...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.220
He took it right off his neck.

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:04.300
I'll have to introduce you to him sometime.

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:05.710
He's quite a character.

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.100
Yeah, he can afford it.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:10.520
He averages 20 bucks an hour, five hours a night.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:11.690
You figure it out.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:14.120
20 bucks an hour? What does this guy do?

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:15.120
Run a diamond mine?

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:17.500
What diamond mine? All he does is pick up five little cards.

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:19.480
It's his five little cards.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:21.820
Only he knows what they are before he picks them up.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:23.520
That's some job.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:26.650
I know another guy that averages four or five hundred a week,

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:27.830
sometimes more.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:29.980
He'd be willing to split a little.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:33.900
My partner. He's the guy I was thinking about for you.

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:34.910
For me?

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:38.660
All you have to do is drive his car. Think he'd be interested?

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:41.260
What makes you think he want me for a partner?

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:46.160
Personal recommendation. All you gotta do is drive his car.

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:47.940
He does all the work.

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:50.190
What kind of work?

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:53.130
Oh, you know, knock over a gas station,

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.310
maybe a hamburger joint or liquor store. Nothing risky.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.530
Oh, no, no. Oh, wait a minute, Jerry.

00:13:58.670 --> 00:13:59.510
I didn't know that you would.

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:06.420
I've done a lot of things in my time, but...

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:06.920
Suit yourself.

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:10.010
He's trying to get you a break. You asked me, didn't you?

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:11.850
Well, yes, I asked you, but I...

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:14.420
Well, what? Anybody else make any better off a lady?

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:19.280
He's killed me. The kick in the teeth, the more they kick her, the better you like her.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:21.750
What are you looking for? Handouts?

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:24.800
Yeah. That's ten bucks. Live.

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:27.810
Don't get sore, Jerry.

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:29.590
Who's sore? I feel sorry for you.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.720
I'll tell you Trubb is the First National Bank.

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:33.800
They'll listen to you. They've got a special tough luck department.

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:37.840
Come on, take the ten bucks and get out of here.

00:14:52.420 --> 00:14:55.300
Yeah, he's your friend.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:24.640
Listen, Mr. Yeager, will you do me a favor?

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.420
Will you go over and tell my wife that I won't be home for dinner?

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:29.750
Because I've got to see about a job.

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:35.540
Yeah. Yes, thank you. Thanks very much, Mr. Yeager.

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:36.290
Right.

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:48.390
Is this nervous?

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:50.680
No. Well, maybe.

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:54.120
So was I the first time. You'll get used to it.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.080
Pull up past the joint.

00:15:59.120 --> 00:15:59.780
Keep it in gear.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:04.540
Brilé.

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:58.510
We are it over there that right look who's here Jessie G button up

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:05.970
says joey you're just as tough mister with an old lady and a sick old man when you ain't got that

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:08.610
Oh, shut up.

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:09.850
Don't do it.

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:10.850
Do him.

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:12.460
Lucky I didn't kill you.

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:33.080
What about that guy that came in? Have any trouble?

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:36.560
Nah. I told you, didn't I? I never have any trouble.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:42.290
What'd you do?

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:51.600
Judy? Hiya, Mr. Yeager. Is Judy here?

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:54.030
Yeah. He hit the television.

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:57.360
Come in. No, no, thanks. Just tell Judy I want her, will you?

00:18:57.680 --> 00:18:59.880
Sure. Get out of my way!

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.300
Nobody ever called me a vomit and live.

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:38.650
The picture's almost over.

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:40.600
Tommy, did you get my note?

00:19:41.040 --> 00:19:41.840
I didn't know what time you were back.

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:43.320
Oh, that's all right, honey. Don't worry about it.

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:46.100
Come on. Pretty soon we'll have our own television set.

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:49.090
Howard, you've got a job. Oh, isn't that wonderful?

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:50.850
Tell me about it. Is it a good one?

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:51.450
What do you think?

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:52.330
What?

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:54.560
I got an advance on my salary. Here, don't you want it?

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:57.820
Oh, Howard. Tell me about it, Howard.

00:19:58.290 --> 00:19:59.970
Look, talk about all the luck. I just happened to...

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:02.900
He's a foreman down the Santa Sierra cannery.

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:05.820
Tell him the whole story. He says I can use a guy like you on the night shift.

00:20:05.980 --> 00:20:07.300
50 bucks a week to start.

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:08.990
Oh, you'll be working nights.

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:13.960
What's the difference? How's about something to eat?

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:17.460
Bait. Oh, it's so expensive.

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:19.500
So what? We got a right to live a little, too?

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:22.520
Oh, boy, potato chips, Tommy.

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:24.760
Son, you still want that two-wheeler?

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:26.280
Yeah, the television, too.

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:28.740
Believe me, when your old man says something, he means it.

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:29.460
Never forget that.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.130
Howard, have you been drinking?

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:33.510
Well, just a couple.

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.200
This fellow may kind of celebrate it.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:37.950
Now, Tommy, go wash your hands first.

00:20:40.470 --> 00:20:42.030
Watch, they're not so dirty.

00:20:42.540 --> 00:20:43.920
Well, put the TV set right here.

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:45.300
Oh, Howard.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.980
And this, that would throw this piece of junk out.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:49.060
Silly.

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:52.040
Honey, when we get that television set,

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:54.520
you can have the whole neighborhood in any time you want.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:23.940
You see, Professor, Boogie Woogie is the most scientific of musical forms.

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:27.610
It's the only one that allows the piano player to keep the music going with one hand

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:29.010
and feed himself with the other.

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:33.140
Drinks are on the house, Professor. Don't be coy, anybody.

00:21:33.860 --> 00:21:34.440
Gil, darling.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:39.340
Your dinner looks beautiful.

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:40.580
You look beautiful.

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:43.760
No one.

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.580
A phone, darling. It's for Hal.

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.360
He can take it in the alcove extension.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:49.420
Okay, okay. Hurry up.

00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:52.100
Oh, and listen. I heard Nicholas barking down the street.

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:53.300
Vito must be coming back.

00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:56.920
Hal, telephone for you.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:58.710
Why don't you take it in the alcove?

00:21:58.980 --> 00:21:59.360
Oh, thanks.

00:21:59.680 --> 00:21:59.900
Bye.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.480
I think our great man is almost here.

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:04.620
Honey, honey, shall I invite him over

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:05.860
for the game tomorrow night?

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:08.350
Oh, fine.

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:09.530
Well, why not?

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:11.150
If he's such a mathematical genius,

00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:13.110
he ought to be able to play a little bridge.

00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:17.160
Time and space have met.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:19.620
Ain't it wonderful what the H-bomb has done, professor?

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:21.940
It's made a scientist almost as important

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:23.160
as a good fullback.

00:22:23.280 --> 00:22:24.480
Peter, we thought you were lost.

00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:26.880
Please, no reproaches, my humble apologies.

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:29.880
This little rascal, he led me not home.

00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:34.680
Oh, Nicholas, I thought I told you to bring Dr. Simone straight home.

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:37.160
Yeah, I'll take him down. Oh, don't be too hard on him.

00:22:37.280 --> 00:22:39.720
There are magnets more powerful than duty.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:43.350
In addition to the cat, he met a lovely French poodle.

00:22:43.970 --> 00:22:46.270
That phone call was from Fowler.

00:22:46.410 --> 00:22:48.530
There's been another holdup out on Highway 101.

00:22:49.120 --> 00:22:50.360
Tell Chuck to stop the presses.

00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:56.600
I can no longer take a position removed from the problems of everyday life.

00:22:57.010 --> 00:22:59.850
There are no ivory towers. Hell.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.720
I can't talk business on an empty stomach.

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:02.800
Sherry?

00:23:03.620 --> 00:23:05.700
The recipe we got from that little place in Rome, remember?

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:06.560
El Greco's?

00:23:06.850 --> 00:23:09.750
Before you leave, I'm going to fix you some of their polenta with quail.

00:23:09.830 --> 00:23:10.210
Quail.

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:13.470
I'm grateful for that day you and your man found me.

00:23:14.010 --> 00:23:15.170
First honors, Vito.

00:23:15.390 --> 00:23:15.810
Thank you.

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:17.740
The boy was pretty badly slugged.

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:20.680
How's about going down there with me after the party breaks up?

00:23:20.760 --> 00:23:22.220
Maybe you'd like to do a special feature?

00:23:22.720 --> 00:23:23.420
On a holdup?

00:23:23.810 --> 00:23:24.470
Plates, everybody.

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:25.590
Why not?

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:28.470
You remember that liquor store a couple of nights ago?

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:29.900
At the service station?

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.080
Stick up the day before.

00:23:31.240 --> 00:23:34.140
Two-bit robberies, Hal. Don't try to talk us into a crime wave.

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:35.840
Maybe we're in one and don't know it.

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:38.840
Anyway, our circulation can stand a little crime wave.

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:41.680
Wait a minute, Vi. That's not enough for you. You're a growing girl.

00:23:41.860 --> 00:23:42.700
My diet.

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:46.240
I was under the impression you hired me to write a column, not general news.

00:23:46.530 --> 00:23:48.070
Maybe a bonus would interest you.

00:23:48.770 --> 00:23:51.480
Bonus? You mean money?

00:23:53.270 --> 00:23:55.810
Hal, you know, that might make a petty robbery very significant.

00:23:56.340 --> 00:23:57.700
Say you'll do it for me, Gil.

00:23:58.020 --> 00:23:59.800
You've got a big following in this town.

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:03.290
With your byline on a special series, I could really sell some papers.

00:24:03.510 --> 00:24:04.700
Are you two plotting?

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:07.060
The boss is trying to get me to work tonight for money.

00:24:07.430 --> 00:24:10.290
Oh, don't you dare take Gil away to the office again tonight.

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:13.580
I'm just getting used to him being home nights, and I like it.

00:24:13.920 --> 00:24:16.100
And besides, we do have a house guest.

00:24:16.240 --> 00:24:17.600
But this is important, Helen.

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:19.080
You understand, Doctor.

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:22.310
My mathematical mind suggests an alternative.

00:24:22.810 --> 00:24:25.690
Why couldn't the house guest accompany his host?

00:24:25.830 --> 00:24:27.130
Oh, this wouldn't interest you, Vito.

00:24:27.450 --> 00:24:28.490
Bye, have some mint sauce.

00:24:29.070 --> 00:24:29.970
Hal's discovered we're...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:36.800
in the middle of a crime wave on the contrary all waves light waves sound waves and crime waves

00:24:36.800 --> 00:24:41.530
interest me very much well you see darling i guess i'll have to work tonight if only to entertain

00:24:41.530 --> 00:24:47.450
veto looks like i'm going to be a headline widow again well let's live while we can who wants some

00:24:47.450 --> 00:24:53.210
wine you'll have some wine if you get a lead officers let me know huh yeah we'll get on to

00:24:53.210 --> 00:24:58.790
this guy a lot of out-of-state hoodlums moving into california towns fellas no this looks more

00:24:58.790 --> 00:24:59.930
like some local roughneck.

00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:01.900
Yeah, this guy likes to leave his trademark.

00:25:02.880 --> 00:25:03.420
Smoke, fella?

00:25:04.080 --> 00:25:05.260
Yeah, thanks, Mr. Clendenning.

00:25:11.740 --> 00:25:12.060
Gil!

00:25:13.200 --> 00:25:14.980
Yeah, Hal, get this veto.

00:25:16.550 --> 00:25:21.230
The angle we'll take is there's probably some Eastern gang operating in the community.

00:25:21.470 --> 00:25:22.630
That always makes good copy.

00:25:22.750 --> 00:25:24.790
This is what's known as building up the family trade.

00:25:24.910 --> 00:25:27.490
By the time Hal and I get through, this town will think it's been invaded.

00:25:27.970 --> 00:25:29.390
Uh, Mr. Clendenning...

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:37.500
A lot occurs to me. Isn't this destructive to the public health, this distortion of realistic values?

00:25:37.820 --> 00:25:41.920
It's not that I personally go in for sensationalism, Doctor. I don't.

00:25:42.060 --> 00:25:45.600
If I had my way, I'd minimize crime as much as possible on the paper.

00:25:45.820 --> 00:25:50.520
In that case, wouldn't the digestion of your readers be greatly improved

00:25:50.520 --> 00:25:57.160
if you were to put your editorials on the front page and the crime news on the editorial page?

00:25:57.680 --> 00:25:59.960
How about that, Al? Where's your sense of social respect?

00:26:00.400 --> 00:26:05.810
Oh, I've got my share, but selling newspapers is my business. That's the way I make my living.

00:26:07.440 --> 00:26:08.060
Good night, doctor.

00:26:09.230 --> 00:26:13.670
And don't forget my invitation. I'd be very happy to show you around the plant any time.

00:26:13.870 --> 00:26:14.310
Thank you.

00:26:14.790 --> 00:26:15.430
Good night, Hal.

00:26:19.410 --> 00:26:21.770
Get some gas while we're here. They can use the business now.

00:26:22.160 --> 00:26:23.620
Joe, fill it up, will you?

00:26:23.740 --> 00:26:24.180
Sure thing.

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:28.640
Joe, tell me something.

00:26:29.160 --> 00:26:29.960
Are you yourself...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.000
not afraid of the effect this

00:26:32.000 --> 00:26:34.140
exaggeration of violence will have on your

00:26:34.140 --> 00:26:35.960
readers. Hal's little crime wave?

00:26:36.660 --> 00:26:39.390
Vito, Hal works on a very fundamental

00:26:39.390 --> 00:26:41.290
formula. People love to be scared

00:26:41.290 --> 00:26:43.730
to death. The more you scare them, the more papers

00:26:43.730 --> 00:26:46.140
they buy. If frightened people

00:26:46.140 --> 00:26:48.360
are the measure of newspaper sales,

00:26:48.540 --> 00:26:50.180
it must be a profitable business.

00:27:04.990 --> 00:27:08.860
I'm thinking about that job tomorrow night. It's got me plenty worried.

00:27:09.410 --> 00:27:11.990
Yeah, you're always worried. Listen to what this guy here Stanton says.

00:27:12.580 --> 00:27:16.500
The outbreak of hoodlumism in this county during the past two weeks...

00:27:16.500 --> 00:27:21.440
...is described by Sheriff Demig's office as the work of a flood of expert gunmen.

00:27:21.750 --> 00:27:23.790
How do you like that? We're a flood of expert gunmen.

00:27:24.960 --> 00:27:26.920
We gotta send him our pictures for the front page, huh?

00:27:28.700 --> 00:27:29.980
You know what we can get for it, don't you?

00:27:31.760 --> 00:27:32.720
What? Tomorrow night.

00:27:33.970 --> 00:27:35.090
Sure, but look at the payoff.

00:27:36.580 --> 00:27:38.540
What do we get tonight for risking our rotten necks?

00:27:38.820 --> 00:27:39.960
$24.83.

00:27:40.660 --> 00:27:41.280
That's split.

00:27:42.060 --> 00:27:43.370
This way, bang.

00:27:44.060 --> 00:27:46.140
Once around, we're on easy street.

00:27:47.900 --> 00:27:49.280
That's the only reason I'm going for it.

00:27:50.750 --> 00:27:53.740
And after that, believe. No more.

00:27:57.380 --> 00:27:58.500
You ain't getting chicken on me, are you?

00:27:59.630 --> 00:27:59.970
You'll be the...

00:28:02.320 --> 00:28:02.940
I'll be there.

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:14.020
I'll be there, Jerry.

00:28:14.320 --> 00:28:17.290
I may be a couple of minutes late, but I'll be there.

00:28:18.600 --> 00:28:18.840
Yeah.

00:28:19.040 --> 00:28:29.540
Be like the black.

00:28:36.440 --> 00:28:39.380
Now, these I do like. You got these in her size?

00:28:39.540 --> 00:28:42.760
Oh, no. How? They're much too fancy.

00:28:42.900 --> 00:28:45.870
Why would I wear them? Honey, we're gonna step out one of these Saturday nights.

00:28:46.170 --> 00:28:49.860
Get them in her size, will ya? Look, hon, I gotta get going or often later.

00:28:50.060 --> 00:28:53.250
Buy whatever else you want, huh? Okay. Bye.

00:28:53.450 --> 00:28:57.550
Bye. So long, partner. Bye! Gotcha!

00:28:57.920 --> 00:28:58.940
Don't ever do that, Tom.

00:29:00.410 --> 00:29:02.210
I'm sorry, boy, but you've got to be careful.

00:29:02.350 --> 00:29:05.700
You put somebody's eyes out, okay?

00:29:06.750 --> 00:29:07.350
Okay, Daddy.

00:29:08.250 --> 00:29:28.410
They get me nervous.

00:29:30.510 --> 00:29:32.630
Maybe he'll be late. He could be in there another hour.

00:29:33.410 --> 00:29:35.030
Not him. He's always out by 11.

00:29:37.320 --> 00:29:38.960
Folks must set an alarm clock.

00:29:45.480 --> 00:29:46.340
How will you relax?

00:29:46.910 --> 00:29:48.390
Look, Jerry, keep your hands off.

00:29:48.630 --> 00:29:49.630
I mean it. Don't shove.

00:29:51.440 --> 00:29:53.460
You want us to get your chin out for peanuts the rest of your life?

00:29:53.580 --> 00:29:55.600
Don't you want to get in the big dough, be somebody for a change?

00:29:56.060 --> 00:29:56.880
I'm here, ain't I?

00:29:58.300 --> 00:29:59.450
Yeah, you're here.

00:30:01.530 --> 00:30:03.240
I tell you, right on time.

00:30:04.360 --> 00:30:29.530
Good evening. What's the idea?

00:30:31.020 --> 00:30:31.920
I feel like a ride.

00:30:33.120 --> 00:30:34.160
Yeah, it's just my style.

00:30:34.620 --> 00:30:35.220
Why don't you turn her over?

00:30:35.480 --> 00:30:36.560
Let me hear what she sounds like.

00:30:36.830 --> 00:30:37.330
Look, I...

00:30:37.330 --> 00:30:37.930
Turn her over.

00:30:45.720 --> 00:30:50.420
Ben, get going.

00:30:53.700 --> 00:30:54.320
Straight out, Al.

00:30:59.090 --> 00:30:59.810
Where'd you get the suit?

00:31:00.540 --> 00:31:00.720
Huh?

00:31:01.250 --> 00:31:03.030
The suit. Where'd you get it? Around here?

00:31:03.680 --> 00:31:06.200
Oh, I... I have them made.

00:31:06.470 --> 00:31:07.210
Around here?

00:31:07.930 --> 00:31:08.390
New York.

00:31:11.180 --> 00:31:13.420
You guys should treat yourselves all right, don't you?

00:31:23.800 --> 00:31:27.000
How do you like that?

00:31:35.920 --> 00:31:38.980
What are you tying me up for? My wallet's in my back pocket. There's $20 in it.

00:31:39.360 --> 00:31:40.300
$20, huh?

00:31:42.740 --> 00:31:44.160
You ought to be able to do better than that.

00:31:44.740 --> 00:31:46.980
If we ask your old man real nice, he'd do a lot better.

00:31:47.770 --> 00:31:49.110
Yes, indeed, a lot better.

00:31:49.230 --> 00:31:50.390
What's my father got to do with this?

00:31:51.190 --> 00:31:58.950
Say, ah, open your mouth. Let me know if it's too tight.

00:31:59.330 --> 00:31:59.970
Come on, get in.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:00.100
Thank you.

00:32:51.120 --> 00:32:58.200
movies oh I told him that last night I'll be nice Johnny it's late I gotta get back

00:33:00.760 --> 00:33:02.100
Okay, have it your own way.

00:33:02.200 --> 00:33:03.600
Oh, wait, Johnny, wait.

00:33:03.900 --> 00:33:05.480
You can see me third, be honest, honey.

00:33:05.600 --> 00:33:06.780
You can follow me third today.

00:33:07.390 --> 00:33:15.710
So nobody's been up here since the war, huh?

00:33:32.840 --> 00:33:33.340
Hold his feet.

00:33:34.370 --> 00:33:35.830
Aren't we going to take him in there, you said?

00:33:35.830 --> 00:33:36.670
Hold his feet.

00:33:36.910 --> 00:33:41.450
He's around here one night.

00:33:41.490 --> 00:33:42.450
He'll come around here any night.

00:33:43.460 --> 00:33:44.400
But where are we going to take him?

00:33:44.420 --> 00:33:45.540
Will you quit talking so much?

00:33:45.780 --> 00:33:49.210
We have that jackpot.

00:34:02.200 --> 00:34:03.060
Jerry, what are you going to do?

00:34:03.200 --> 00:34:03.800
Jerry, don't!

00:34:04.930 --> 00:34:06.730
You do that again and I'll break in half.

00:34:06.890 --> 00:34:08.490
What's the matter with you anyhow, you his brother or something?

00:34:08.690 --> 00:34:10.710
Jerry, you never said you were going to kill him.

00:34:10.770 --> 00:34:11.610
Why do you have to kill him?

00:34:11.650 --> 00:34:12.990
You want him to give our description to the cops?

00:34:13.490 --> 00:34:14.730
What do they do when they get that chance?

00:34:14.890 --> 00:34:16.030
I got more brains than any of them.

00:34:16.680 --> 00:34:18.280
You hear me, I got more brains than any of you.

00:34:19.020 --> 00:34:21.200
Jerry, don't you dare to look like I just like that.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:35.320
Let me get his truck.

00:34:38.200 --> 00:34:38.420
Watch.

00:34:40.370 --> 00:34:40.830
That's your right.

00:34:41.440 --> 00:34:42.200
Cops will have a description.

00:34:43.010 --> 00:34:43.410
Too bad.

00:34:46.380 --> 00:34:47.870
Yeah, this is Ty Clip.

00:34:48.620 --> 00:34:49.700
You gotta have something to send with a ransom note.

00:34:50.350 --> 00:34:52.150
You didn't say you're gonna still try to collect?

00:34:52.770 --> 00:34:53.670
What are you talking about?

00:34:54.200 --> 00:34:55.480
You think I slugged him just for the fun of it?

00:34:55.580 --> 00:34:56.240
Put it in your pocket.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:00.820
20 bucks, all right.

00:35:02.870 --> 00:35:04.110
All right, let's get him into the water.

00:35:05.180 --> 00:35:06.760
Come on, come on, we ain't got all night.

00:36:17.420 --> 00:36:20.420
You woke me up. What time is it?

00:36:23.070 --> 00:36:23.530
1.30.

00:36:30.990 --> 00:36:36.330
I was having the most wonderful dream.

00:36:38.060 --> 00:36:39.880
I was in hospital having the baby.

00:36:41.180 --> 00:36:42.560
This time it didn't hurt at all.

00:36:44.800 --> 00:36:46.300
I said, Daddy, the minute she was born.

00:36:50.320 --> 00:36:50.900
My back.

00:37:01.020 --> 00:37:02.440
You do want a girl, don't you?

00:37:04.360 --> 00:37:09.020
Yeah. You sure there's no pain?

00:37:10.560 --> 00:37:11.900
Don't lie to me, no. I want to know.

00:37:12.990 --> 00:37:14.790
No, I'm all right, Howard. I feel fine.

00:37:25.220 --> 00:37:26.040
What's the matter, Howard?

00:37:28.350 --> 00:37:28.870
Nothing, why?

00:37:30.090 --> 00:37:30.690
My hands are trembling.

00:37:33.390 --> 00:37:34.450
Felt a little cold.

00:37:38.520 --> 00:37:39.160
Much better.

00:37:41.320 --> 00:37:43.000
She had the biggest blue eyes.

00:37:43.600 --> 00:37:44.560
Just like a picture.

00:37:45.370 --> 00:37:47.790
I got right up out of the hospital and took her shopping.

00:37:49.390 --> 00:37:49.850
Isn't that funny?

00:37:52.100 --> 00:37:53.360
We went to the same store.

00:37:53.950 --> 00:37:55.370
I bought the dressing today.

00:37:56.920 --> 00:37:58.500
I was buying her a pinafore.

00:39:47.690 --> 00:39:51.490
Gracie, bring me another order of them French fried onions, huh?

00:39:51.970 --> 00:39:53.390
One bicarb coming up.

00:39:53.670 --> 00:39:59.340
Here, Ben. I said 5.30.

00:40:02.910 --> 00:40:04.830
Didn't I tell you to quit slopping on that shellac?

00:40:04.930 --> 00:40:05.830
You wanna get osus or something?

00:40:06.760 --> 00:40:07.460
What'd you eat today?

00:40:07.850 --> 00:40:08.490
I ate...

00:40:08.770 --> 00:40:09.070
What?

00:40:09.290 --> 00:40:09.690
Soup.

00:40:10.200 --> 00:40:11.180
You call that eating?

00:40:12.000 --> 00:40:12.920
Bring him a steak, Tracy.

00:40:13.460 --> 00:40:14.100
No, I don't want it.

00:40:14.240 --> 00:40:15.300
How's about a steak sandwich?

00:40:16.060 --> 00:40:17.020
Yeah, give it to him.

00:40:17.700 --> 00:40:19.020
Bring him a cup of coffee first.

00:40:19.590 --> 00:40:20.610
He don't feel so good.

00:40:21.470 --> 00:40:22.690
One cow on a slab.

00:40:27.840 --> 00:40:28.820
That's our insurance policy.

00:40:30.190 --> 00:40:31.090
Take a look at it.

00:41:05.240 --> 00:41:08.420
